From: Dainis Gorbunovs <9624041+DainisGorbunovs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:01:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] 10169: Decompiler: prevent Max-Payload integer overflow

DecompileProcess converted the "Decompiler Max-Payload (MBytes)" option to
bytes with an int shift, so large values wrapped to unrelated limits: 2048 MB
became negative and 4096 MB became zero, rejecting every response including
the one that registers the program, while 4097 MB silently became 1 MB.
Widen to long before shifting; the response buffers already take a long
limit.
---
 .../src/main/java/ghidra/app/decompiler/DecompileProcess.java   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/decompiler/DecompileProcess.java b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/decompiler/DecompileProcess.java
index 5752ae88f3..852b426b54 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/decompiler/DecompileProcess.java
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/main/java/ghidra/app/decompiler/DecompileProcess.java
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@ public class DecompileProcess {
 					// start with any initial allocation of 1024 bytes, also give an absolute upper bound
 					// determined by maxResultSizeMBYtes
 					currentResponse = mainResponse;
-					currentResponse.open(maxResultSizeMBYtes << 20, programSource);
+					currentResponse.open((long) maxResultSizeMBYtes << 20, programSource);
 					break;
 				case 15:			// This is the end of the main decompiler output
 					if (currentResponse == null) {
-- 
